<sup><b>1</b></sup> If <i>it had not been</i> the Lord who was on our side, now may Israel say;<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> If <i>it had not been</i> the Lord who was on our side, when men rose up against us:<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> Then they had swallowed us up quick, when their wrath was kindled against us:<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> Then the waters had overwhelmed us, the stream had gone over our soul:<br />
<sup><b>5</b></sup> Then the proud waters had gone over our soul.<br />
<sup><b>6</b></sup> Blessed <i>be</i> the Lord, who hath not given us <i>as</i> a prey to their teeth.<br />
<sup><b>7</b></sup> Our soul is escaped as a bird out of the snare of the fowlers: the snare is broken, and we are escaped.<br />
<sup><b>8</b></sup> Our help <i>is</i> in the name of the Lord, who made heaven and earth. <br />
